{composer:  Paul Simon  }


https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sD9SqfEKlLsy2imfVjLyOivaIYqTfQ5_/view?usp=sharing  (Capo 7)

This version is just how Paul performs it live, capo'd at the 7th fret.  Another live version is uncapo'd.  That version is probably slightly easier to play but lacks some of the nuanced finger work.  Also available are the album versions, one capo'd at the 4th fret which has the (Bm).  The other album version is capo'd at the 6th fret and does not.

TIP:  It looks like a mess down there but it's not!  It's pretty darn easy to play and sounds wonderful.  So just read through and give it a go.

TIP:  So the intro is picked.  Form (Asus2) which is just (A) without the bottom string and pick the notes (notes may or may not transpose), which are 3rd string, 1st string, 2nd string, and 1st string again.  Finish the sequence with a rake of the |Asus2| from the top string down to the 3rd string.

TIP:  Okay so now there are 3 sets of voicings to get down and they're all easy.  The first is the (G) - (G4) - (G).  From (G) just move your index finger from the 5th string to the 2nd string and back.  The ring finger can stay on the top string if you want.  Next is the (Am) - (Asus2) - (Am).  From the (Am) just lift off the index finger and replace it.  Finally there's the (C) - (Cmaj7) - (C).  From the (C) just remove your index finger and replace it.  See?  Freakin' easy.  Suggest downstrokes for each one.


